{
  "title": "Impending Fracture & Prophylactic Fixation",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8002/impending-fracture-and-prophylactic-fixation",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 28 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Criteria for prophylactic fixation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Several methods exist to predict the risk of pathologic fracture. These include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the presence of significant functional pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "> 50% destruction of cortical bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "formal staging systems",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Harington's criteria",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Mirels' criteria",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prophylactic fixation is preferred to fixation of actual pathological fracture due to",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "shorter operative time",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "decreased morbidity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "quicker recovery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Harington's criteria",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Haringtons' Criteria",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "> 50% destruction of diaphyseal cortices",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "> 50-75% destruction of metaphysis (> 2.5 cm)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Permeative destruction of the subtrochanteric femoral region",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Persistent pain following irradiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
